# id <TAB> kind <TAB> scope <TAB> site <TAB> quote. One row per construct the pinned xacro
# dispatches on, derived by walking the syntax tree of its own source rather than listed:
# a tag an element's name is compared against outside an assert, the attribute list a tag
# checks, a lexer token, an element of the valid substitution commands, a special form, a
# raised exception and a warning, which are the kinds tag, attrs, token, command, form,
# raise and warning. The scope is that of the outermost enclosing function or class:
# expression for upstream's ${} expression surface, tool for the command-line driver, and
# grammar for every other site, so a site moved between them changes its row. The site is
# module:line in the pinned source. The quote is the literal the row derives from; an
# attribute list quotes required=a,b optional=c, and a raise site its exception class and
# its message up to the first placeholder that follows a word. The id is the kind and
# the literal, or for an attribute list the tag it checks, lowercased with every run of
# other characters an underscore; a message with no words is named instead by the raised
# class and the function, or by the function alone for a warning. A second site with the
# same id takes its function's name and a third its line. A quote escapes a
# backslash, a tab and a newline as \\, \t and \n. Rows are ordered by module, line and id.
